<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU pulls sponsorship from Disinfo2026 event in Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56a4dfd2a0fe958f34fa692e291885863af8c354bb72821304f814cf3fe6b6b6</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615--b060dac4b016.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's diplomatic service, Canada and host nation Lithuania all pulled support from a disinformation event in Vilnius. Amid reports of US pressure, the EU said it was "uncomfortable with the framing" of some panels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Security in the Black Sea region: is Bulgaria the weak link in Europe's defense against threats from Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbee76b7b85358d49d2cded64909c5ad1ca0bf532e19774dcf355a42a5642388</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-/a-79592663--cd93d129d2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-russia/a-79592663?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two ships have sunk off the coast of Bulgaria and Romania after drone attacks in recent days. Bulgaria has held back on pointing the finger at Russia. What does that mean for security in the Black Sea and the region?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea recalls Ukraine ambassador amid POW dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0848b1d7b87c55e5c1b5cc5b5d938c25eee238b2cebd2495c01a617370290d4a</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511--9732a38bcd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has said it will recall its ambassador to Ukraine. Seoul is upset about a transfer of North Korean prisoners of war being made public knowledge at the UN and had demanded — but not received — an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian data centers, could Ukraine soon be offline?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b80f86f563a3c4d9a41c5887f8393c25dcdb7857ed9994ccbcab2606d8106527</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503--ed9380350022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia targets Ukraine's data centers more and more, experts say the country's internet system is too robust to shut down entirely. However, services could become more expensive.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Middle Corridor: Can Bulgaria be a safe gateway for Asian imports to the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1fef6254dc311fdbf4b166f913d93bfad2b3a11513e9f96524d2fa9ae08f339</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530--0deecfdaf02f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants more trade via the Middle Corridor, which could bring big benefits for Bulgaria. But Tuesday's drone attacks on commercial ships off the Bulgarian coast are a stark reminder of the security risks involved.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gerhard Schröder visits latest Russian employer, Hyperglobus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cc224716cc7a71a3934aca196bf1247df70a93c8c8637d90476485415569149</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schr_der-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018--1d88da466f5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schröder-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder visited a Moscow supermarket in his new role on the supervisory board. Schröder is no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: European Commission tables reforms to prepare bloc for new members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aca65614bf042488574e345c9743deb3d0422549a2a8c06b8559f09f6486b936</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493--0237e634d1b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission is proposing earlier access to EU markets for candidate countries, new voting rules to reduce vetoes and extra safeguards for a bigger bloc. But is the reform fair — or even feasible?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:052161c43fed9a2043fc20a2efd73ab27991c155600acc1d4956486d286d1a6d</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Where is Spain headed after the snap election announcement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:154fc35a790bf38cffee7f342f01925a3cebca35c64bcd86f09e7358b3f5bf04</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959--1490181fc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is taking a gamble by calling an early election in Spain. The housing crisis, migration and the rise of the right-wing populist Vox party are all likely to dominate the campaign.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks ways to make expansion more palatable to members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:968141e2c982370a77eb34e20e397ae5a67780951476b1b3c0c025504182d805</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297--4cde5d079d87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has put forward ideas it hopes will both ease the EU expansion process and allay concerns among existing members. Several countries, not least war-torn Ukraine, are among the candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's conundrum: How to cut spending amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c3588aa6042eb6992ece7c603b54f491c9c5e4205dc9b4e0b27efb5ae500ec1</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475--ca64b77315f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Lecornu is pledging to improve schools at a time when the government seeks to save billions. France's dilemma can be seen across the EU: How to cut spending when citizens are demanding more from the state?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Misleading claims spark plague fears in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc53e1c0f3f43c82fb498c0d53109bd5d1e385730dc5f8b635dcab90043fe6b8</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752--eaca60a52c9c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-misleading-claims-spark-plague-fears-in-russia/a-79560752?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of a lab worker at a plague research institute in Russia has sparked claims about a lab accident, hundreds of infections and international spread. Some of these viral narratives are misleading.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfb1b7d90033ef1e62b90041f7790ec0e333076a82d667a570d879125f1b00ad</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia election: New steps to prevent electoral fraud, but nationalist parties remain on top</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55991989a03c5e76a7d7918094eb1fd4e12946ed886771dc31329a5e51a8062d</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717--5102b97990e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New technology has stopped votes being cast on behalf of dead or absent voters, and turnout has fallen to a record low. But it was a case of deja vu in Bosnia's elections with the same parties winning.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of French schools shut, teen loses hand in protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ebed528f4b866fd0e29aa3d289a8e3b4d6faaecb6b7abbc3ba976690e35382a</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656--d9ec9cc932b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student protests that rocked France last week have prompted authorities to keep up to 500 schools closed on Monday. A teenage boy lost his hand, seemingly while trying to pick up a police tear gas grenade.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nationalists top Bosnia-Herzegovina's divisive election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cdebc2737319af5a8bae3209bb33cba5fe080cb0246d16915b80bff849c3f81</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T22:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nationalists-top-bosnia-herzegovina-s-divisive-election/a-79535336--ff55c4d27908.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nationalists-top-bosnia-herzegovina-s-divisive-election/a-79535336?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia-Herzegovina's three-member presidency is set to be dominated by nationalists from the three major ethnic groups, including Zeljka ​Cvijanovic, backed by disqualified Serb secessionist leader Milorad Dodik.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK remands 2 Iranians over alleged antisemitic terror plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b60848aa210acb404d587c0fa727d957d205ec8bc70cc61fb64e921fc20c7fe</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T16:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-remands-2-iranians-over-alleged-antisemitic-terror-plot/a-79532184--b38b3689556f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-remands-2-iranians-over-alleged-antisemitic-terror-plot/a-79532184?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pair were arrested on the eve of Yom Kippur and later charged with plotting to attack Jewish targets in Manchester.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia and Herzegovina is still shaped by war, separatism, EU ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f921413b1f4650629510185e60b17dc47a467f9227d6e1824f3f5013bfa5bb4b</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-is-still-shaped-by-war-separatism-eu-ambitions/a-79523557--c6b59bb6d492.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-is-still-shaped-by-war-separatism-eu-ambitions/a-79523557?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia and Herzegovina is governed by a system established after the Bosnian war — more than 30 years ago. Ethnic divisions, a complex administration and European integration all shape the country's political reality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Spain's parliament rejects housing bill as protests continue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c6562be3d15071e29b7dd2faa6d0b49762e0305ea07bc4962934ec37e5e0b9a</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683--f3b2b2f36991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's minority government suffered defeat in parliament as it tried to push through a pair of emergency measures aimed at making housing more affordable. A pensioner's eviction and protests led to the bid.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, South Korea clash over transfer of 2 North Korean prisoners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b489c7b10c9ce9a45b8e22e9945986fea386fea06ee4fe4a4b4e5869fddb32db</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-clash-over-transfer-of-2-north-korean-prisoners/a-79508601--363762584d93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-clash-over-transfer-of-2-north-korean-prisoners/a-79508601?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A diplomatic scandal has erupted over two North Korean prisoners of war, with South Korea demanding an apology from Ukraine. What's been the reaction in Kyiv?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
